  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "R01",
      "locator": "22_CLIENT_INTERFACE_DETAILS.md:76,151-153",
      "fact": "session.control target must belong to current session Goal/Run. Resume requires valid paused/recovery context, cancelled Run not revived; explicit continuation may create provenance-preserving new attempt/run, retaining original cancellation/budget/failure counts."
    },
    {
      "id": "R02",
      "locator": "internal/domain/client_protocol.go:1120-1149",
      "fact": "Existing special RESUME target=session checks queue/previous terminal stop facts, builds snapshot, returns COMPLETED without checkpoint resume, new attempt or runtime producer."
    },
    {
      "id": "R03",
      "locator": "apps/cli/cli_verbs.go:77-110",
      "fact": "Both CLI resume operation lists send target_id=session. The schema minLength alone does not establish prose-required Goal/Run membership."
    },
    {
      "id": "R04",
      "locator": "internal/domain/durability.go:259-401",
      "fact": "ResumeCheckpoint has its own BeginTx/Commit and token-based SCHEDULER validation. It requires current nonterminal Run/active Task/Goal/checkpoint/trusted stopped observation/effects reconciliation/input/dependency/admission; rebuilds context, rotates lease, carries checkpoint and prepares native dispatch if native. Terminal/cancel-requested cannot use it."
    },
    {
      "id": "R05",
      "locator": "internal/domain/client_protocol_sessions.go:14-20",
      "fact": "ClientSessionRuntime interface exposes only sameTx ValidateBinding/AdmitTurn; comments prohibit launch/provider requests/second Tx. Calling public ResumeCheckpoint inside this interface or envelope Tx would violate the existing transaction boundary."
    }
  ],
  "implementation_obligations": [
    "Resolve lawful current Goal/Run target from authoritative snapshot and original membership; refuse session-id target or wrong/foreign/obsolete identity with typed error, without manufacturing execution.",
    "Define actual PAUSE checkpoint/stop reconciliation producer and RESUME admission/new attempt routes separately from snapshot observation; determine exact worker/coordinator/bridge support before claiming a closed file list.",
    "Retain CANCELLED Run and immutable old command/effect/budget/failure/event facts; never nested-call token service methods in current client Tx and never relabel permanent ACK or snapshot-only COMPLETED as recovery.",
    "Protect old22/23 controls, F08 sameTx finalization scope and history/LIVE held lanes. Before edits, freeze exact path/function/producer/control/native selectors and obtain nonauthor scope review plus Root canonical registration."
  ],
